                  "width": 420,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 12,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "t47MHg",
                      "name": "Caption",
                      "fill": "$text-tertiary",
                      "content": "Resolution & pins",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                      "fontSize": "$text-xs",
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "h90XJC",
                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A frame's Theme section pins axes for its subtree; Inherit removes the pin. Library axes appear as alias:axis and default from the library. Instances pin exactly the same way (Theme section in the instance inspector, see 11).",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": "$text-sm",
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "lFpkQ",
                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A value cell matches when every axis it names equals the effective value; unnamed axes are ignored. Among matches the last entry wins. — means no entry for that axis.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": "$text-sm",
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "wEzFU",
                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "An alias chip is a {\"$ref\"} binding; it must point at a variable of the same type. Detach keeps the resolved literal.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": "$text-sm",
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "PgVk9",
                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Colors keep their space: OKLCH and Display-P3 values are stored as written and gamut-mapped only for display; the swatch corner flags out-of-sRGB values.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": "$text-sm",
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "U8VeI",
                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Variables tab (left panel) is the compact read-and-bind list; the dialog (⌘⇧V) is where values, axes and groups are edited.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": "$text-sm",
